10
00:39:31,428 --> 00:39:37,428
On November 21, 2021, Darrell Edward Brooks Jr.

11
00:43:28,571 --> 00:43:34,571
drove a sport utility vehicle (SUV) through the annual Christmas parade in Waukesha,
Wisconsin, United States, killing six people and injuring 62 others.

12
00:47:25,714 --> 00:47:31,714
The parade was live-streamed, and other attendees captured the
incident on videos later posted to social media.

13
00:51:22,857 --> 00:51:28,857
Brooks, who had been reportedly diagnosed with bipolar disorder as a child, had an extensive
criminal record including several charges of sex crimes and domestic violence.

14
00:55:20,000 --> 00:55:26,000
He pleaded not guilty to six counts of first-degree
intentional homicide and 70 additional charges.

15
00:59:17,142 --> 00:59:23,142
He chose to represent himself at his trial, which began on October 3, 2022.

16
01:03:14,285 --> 01:03:20,285
Brooks presented pseudolegal arguments from the sovereign citizen movement and was repeatedly
removed from the courtroom for failing to comply with decorum and courtesy.

17
01:07:11,428 --> 01:07:17,428
On October 26, 2022, a jury found Brooks guilty on all 76 charges.

18
01:11:08,571 --> 01:11:14,571
On November 16, 2022, he was sentenced to six consecutive life sentences without the
possibility of parole, plus an additional 762.5 years to be served consecutively.

19
01:15:05,714 --> 01:15:11,714
The film explores themes of small town, holiday, christmas, christmas parade.

